      "side": 1,
      "message": "None these texture builtin issues are \"A small deviation in output\". A small deviation in output is \"1.2 + 0.1 \u003d 1.3 +/i 0.1\"\n\nThese are bugs. As one example sampling texture arrays in Mac Intel always samples array layer 0. That\u0027s not small deviation in output.\n\nSimilarly with offset bugs. Offsets are integer offsets. Indexing an array with `someArray[v + 3]` that doesn\u0027t give you element `v + 3` is a bug, not a \"small deviation in output\".\n\nYou don\u0027t know what the offsets are used for. You can\u0027t assume it\u0027s a minor visual glitch since you can\u0027t know that the offsets are used for visual calculations instead of financial or medical calculations.",
      "revId": "6cb839138a48fe868e879a629aee893b05238991",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
